    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on stolen base efficiency and high-upside matchups. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (79.13) headlines our offensive attack; while facing a respectable arm in Luis Castillo, the combination of his top-of-the-order positioning and a +14% platoon edge makes him our most potent asset. **Trea Turner** (74.58) and **Kyle Schwarber** (73.46) follow closely behind in the efficiency rankings, both benefiting significantly from a favorable matchup against Junk. The high scores for **Junior Caminero** (70.15) and **Caleb Durbin** (67.03) are driven by positive park factors and vulnerable opposing starters, though **Caleb Durbin** carries a slight caveat with a 30% rain risk that we will need to monitor throughout the afternoon.\n\nRegarding roster management, **Carson Benge** (58.65) was our most contested start, narrowly edging out depth options. We leaned into **Carson Benge** due to his projected #4 spot in the lineup, which provides a reliable RBI floor that our bench depth lacks today. Conversely, the weather-related uncertainty surrounding **Lars Nootbaar** (50.13) suppressed his total score, making him a marginal play; should the weather shift further, we have players like **Nelson Velazquez** or **Josh Smith** ready to step into the fray to protect our limited game caps. While **Dillon Dingler** (45.71) carries a lower score due to a dynamic platoon disadvantage, he remains locked in as our primary catcher, as his elite frame time remains a staple of our defensive strategy even on days where his offensive ceiling is capped.",
